$\\textrm{Var}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=3\\big]$ given that the conditional probability mass function $f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, 3)$ is shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is $\\mu_{Y|3} = \\dfrac{8}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188034 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6cdc2b0e-a968-5d95-8fb6-5d469a5920b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188034 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=3] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)]-{\\mu }_{Y|3}^{2} \\\\  & =[(1)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+(2)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}+(4)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}]-{(\\frac{8}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}+8-\\frac{64}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188035 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10306" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188035 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{16}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\textrm{Var}\\big[X \\,|\\, Y=2\\big]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is $\\mu_{X|2}=\\dfrac{10}{9}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188035 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "49a039ae-dbe1-5faa-a9a7-014bd9549c03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188035 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find $f_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{16}$ |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $\\dfrac{9}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{7}{16}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\nf_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y)  = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_Y(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y{:}$\n\n| $f_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{8}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{4}{7}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{7}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)]-{\\mu }_{X|2}^{2} \\\\  & =[{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{8}{9}+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}]-{(\\frac{10}{9})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9}+\\frac{4}{9}-\\frac{100}{81} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{81}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188046 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10352" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188046 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{3}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\textrm{Var}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=1\\big]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is $\\mu_{Y|1} = \\dfrac{9}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188046 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3764cb54-7fd2-584a-9dc7-eda88368b032" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188046 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find $f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | $f_X(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{5}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{3}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\nf_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x)  = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_X(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x{:}$\n\n| $f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =[{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{3}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}]-{(\\frac{9}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+1+\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{81}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188327 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188327 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188327 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186188634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188327 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186188635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188327 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186527927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188327 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186527950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] 