\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =[(0)^{2}\\cdot 0.1+(1)^{2}\\cdot 0.4+(2)^{2}\\cdot 0.5]-(1.4)^{2} \\\\  & =0+0.4+2-1.96 \\\\  & =0.44.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188637 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186186102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188637 #edb/ref 1069 "q-145581" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188637 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188637 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|0}=\\frac{1}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188637 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "87429b89-e333-5492-85d9-bf5d6ddc4038" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188637 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188637 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given 