s first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=0] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|0}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}]-{(1)}^{2} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{2}+1-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188689 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186186414 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188689 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146289" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188689 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188689 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|0}=\\frac{13}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188689 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "07c19340-2d1a-5056-9657-cee2e32e9b96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188689 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188689 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{9}{20}$ | $\\frac{11}{20}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{4}{11}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{4}{9}$ | $\\frac{5}{11}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{11}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)]-{\\mu }_{X|0}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{9}+{3}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{9}+{9}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}]-{(\\frac{13}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =0+4+27-\\frac{169}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{110}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189167 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189167 #edb/ref 1061 38837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189167 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2ef086e9-8163-573e-9575-a78051c9420a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189167 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189168 #edb/ref 1061 38849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189168 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ac37dad4-4109-5b6c-a2d0-f6c46e058597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189168 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189169 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189169 #edb/ref 1061 38850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189169 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "12bb1f79-4af3-56c1-b495-e654c2cf5d1c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189169 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186189401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189183 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189183 #edb/ref 1061 38984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189183 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7f447a96-6d58-5356-934d-4d4a94738359" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189183 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189401 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables, where the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is given by $\\mu_{X|y}.$ In other words,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] = \\mu_{X|y}.\n$$\n\nThe **conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$** is defined as\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] = \\textrm{E}\\big[(X - \\mu_{X|y} \\big)^2 \\,|\\, Y=y].\n$$\n\nThis is similar to the definition of $\\textrm{Var}[X]$ in that it represents the average  (squared) distance of the random variable $X$ from the mean. The difference here is that the expected values are now dependent on the outcome of $Y.$\n\nSimilarly to the case of $\\textrm{Var}[X],$ this often isn't the easiest formula to use in practice. However, it can be shown that the definition of conditional variance is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f_{X|Y}(x \\,|\\, y)$ is the conditional PMF of $X$ given $Y.$ Note that these formulas are analogous to those for $\\textrm{Var}[X].$\n\nFinally, we have an analogous definition for the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189401 #edb/ref 1065 6431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189401 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ce4fb1c3-94ee-51c3-b10d-ce6ea0c7ff38" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189401 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510755 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186511586 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510755 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186511606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510755 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186511621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510755 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186511666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510755 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186511670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510755 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510755 #edb/ref 1045 "Conditional Variance for Discrete Random Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510755 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186511586 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510755 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510755 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510755 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "2295589f-1938-53e1-a9aa-ded9c732eec7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510824 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510824 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510824 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "14738cb2-b471-5d99-b3eb-4afbb5fa348a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510853 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510853 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510853 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "20ae5337-49f2-5726-8ce9-b